@startuml sequence
!include style.puml
title A day's steps reaching Apple Health

participant "BridgeService\non the watch" as SVC #EAF8EF
participant "BridgeCentral" as BC #EAF2FC
participant "HealthStore" as STORE #EAF2FC
participant "HealthKitSink" as SINK #EAF2FC
participant "Apple Health" as HK #F2F2F7

== Bringing the link up ==

SVC -> SVC : advertise, 30s burst / 5min rest
BC -[#0A6ED1]> SVC : connect with the bond keys
BC -> SVC : discover services
BC -> SVC : subscribe by writing the CCCD
SVC -> SVC : advertising off
BC -> SVC : sync, goal
note over SVC, BC
  Encrypted and MITM protected, or the watch
  refuses the read, the write and the subscribe.
end note

== Steady state ==

SVC -[#1DA34A]> BC : day: absolute total for the watch's own date
SVC -[#B23A34]> BC : hr: one reading every 5s

== Mirroring one day ==

BC -> STORE : day record, N steps
STORE -> SINK : sum the samples we wrote for that date
SINK -> HK : statistics query, our source only
HK --> SINK : M steps
note right of SINK
  An empty date comes back as errorNoData.
  That is a sum of zero, not a failure. Reading
  it as a failure meant the first sample of a
  new day was never written, so the date stayed
  empty and the query kept failing.
end note

alt N > M
  STORE -[#1DA34A]> SINK : write N minus M
  SINK -[#1DA34A]> HK : one step sample
else N < M
  STORE -> SINK : delete our samples, write N
  SINK -> HK : the day, replaced
else store sealed or not authorised
  SINK --> STORE : errorDatabaseInaccessible
  STORE -> STORE : keep the day queued
  note right of STORE
    Retried on the next push, on unlock, on an
    authorisation change, and on foreground.
  end note
end

== When the day pushes stop ==

BC -> BC : 20 minutes without a day
BC -> SVC : sync, as a probe
BC -> BC : 25 minutes without a day
BC -[#B23A34]> SVC : drop the connection
note over BC, SVC
  Reconnecting forces a fresh discovery and a fresh
  CCCD write, which is what the watch is waiting for.
end note
@enduml
